{
  "$comment": [
    "The site's navigation, in one place, read by two renderers.",
    "",
    "The app shell is rendered twice: once by React (web/components/shell/Sidebar.tsx)",
    "for the twelve Next routes, and once as a string template by the Python fund-page",
    "generator (pipeline/pipeline/fund_pages.py) for the 9,016 generated documents, which",
    "ship no React at all. Before this file the two copies of the nav were maintained by",
    "hand and were already free to drift; now both read this file and",
    "web/components/shell/nav.test.ts compares their rendered output.",
    "",
    "JSON rather than TypeScript so Python can load it with json.load and no parser.",
    "",
    "`match` is a list of path prefixes. A path matches an entry when it equals the",
    "prefix, equals the prefix plus a slash, or starts with the prefix plus a slash;",
    "`/` matches only itself. The first match wins, so no two entries may overlap.",
    "",
    "`icon` is the `d` attribute of a 24x24 stroked path, so both renderers draw the",
    "same glyph from the same bytes."
  ],
